From multi-cluster architecture to multi-team boundaries, I’ve implemented these patterns across several production environments.

When you're managing multiple teams, environments, or clusters, GitOps can either become a mess — or your secret weapon for consistency.

Here’s how we design multi-tenant GitOps setups using ArgoCD 👇

🧩 Multi-Tenant Patterns:
1. ArgoCD Projects
✅ Isolate teams/apps with scoped RBAC
✅ Control allowed repos, namespaces, clusters

2. Namespace-per-Tenant
Logical separation for team-specific workloads

3. App of Apps for Each Group
Let teams manage their own root app — modular, autonomous, Git-native

🌍 Multi-Cluster GitOps:
Use ArgoCD Instances per cluster, or

Central ArgoCD managing multiple clusters via kubeconfigs

✅ Combine with external secrets + policies
✅ Use sync waves to orchestrate cross-cluster apps

🧠 Pro Tip:
Use tooling like ArgoCD ApplicationSets with generators (Git, List, Cluster) to dynamically create apps for each environment or tenant.

📌 TL;DR
More clusters ≠ more chaos.
Design GitOps systems that scale with your platform.
